= Melacus Branch

Melacus is an industrial city built around its central foundry, specializing in the production of low-tech hardware and structural components, from basic bolts and screws to heavy steel and titanium plating.

Predictably, the local party section is dominated by leftist figures, primarily trade unionists and moderate communists. Over time, this branch has forged a strong relationship of goodwill and mutual trust with the local {!<span style="color: #540808;"><strong>PLFM</strong></span>!} section, regularly coordinating on labor strikes and community organizing.

- @work_with_plfm
